
# 🧬 NCBI Protein Sequence Retrieval

This directory contains manually retrieved NCBI Protein sequence datasets organized into subfolders for downstream computational analysis, amino acid sequence alignment, and molecular docking prep.

---

## 📂 Directory Structure

```text
Protein_Sequence/
├── NP_000509.1/         # Human Hemoglobin Subunit Beta (HBB) protein data
├── NP_007295.1/         # Human BRCA1 tumor suppressor protein data
├── NP_032110.1/         # Mouse GAPDH metabolic enzyme protein data
├── NP_415492.1/         # E. coli K-12 DNA Polymerase I protein data
└── YP_009724390.1/      # SARS-CoV-2 Spike Glycoprotein data

```
## 🔬 Dataset Overview

Each accession folder contains local protein sequence files (FASTA / GenPept formats) representing core model proteins across viral, bacterial, mouse, and human biology:

| Accession Folder | Organism | Protein Name | Length | Biological Relevance |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **`NP_000509.1`** | *Homo sapiens* | Hemoglobin Subunit Beta (**HBB**) | 147 aa | Oxygen transport & point mutation analysis (e.g., Sickle Cell) |
| **`NP_007295.1`** | *Homo sapiens* | BRCA1 DNA Repair Associated | 1,863 aa | Tumor suppressor protein & DNA repair mechanisms |
| **`NP_032110.1`** | *Mus musculus* | Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase (**GAPDH**) | 333 aa | Housekeeping enzyme & metabolic control baseline |
| **`NP_415492.1`** | *E. coli* K-12 | DNA Polymerase I (**PolA**) | 928 aa | Prokaryotic DNA replication & repair machinery |
| **`YP_009724390.1`** | *SARS-CoV-2* | Spike Glycoprotein (**S**) | 1,273 aa | Host ACE2 receptor binding & molecular docking target |

---

## 🛠️ Applications & Usage

* **Local Protein Parsing:** Facilitates offline reading of FASTA headers, amino acid sequences, and GenPept feature annotations without querying NCBI APIs.
* **Structural & Computational Modeling:** Provides input sequences for secondary structure prediction, physicochemical profiling (e.g., via Biopython's `ProteinAnalysis`), homology modeling, and molecular docking preparation.

